{
  "title": "Deep Peroneal Nerve Entrapment",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7043/deep-peroneal-nerve-entrapment",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Dec 9 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Deep Peroneal Nerve Entrapment, also called Anterior Tarsal Tunnel Syndrome, is a rare compression neuropathy affecting the deep peroneal nerve, most commonly at the fibro-osseous tunnel formed by the inferior extensor retinaculum.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be suspected clinically with dorsal foot pain with radiation to the 1st webspace and a positive Tinel's sign over the DPN.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is a trial of nonoperative management with shoe modifications. Surgical anterior tarsal tunnel release is indicated in patients with persistent symptoms who fail nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Epidemiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Incidence",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "rare",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Demographics",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "adults of all ages and genders",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Risk factors",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "high heel use",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "compressive shoe wear",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "previous fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathophysiology",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "site of compression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "anterior leg/ankle/foot from 1 cm proximal to ankle joint proximally to talonavicular joint distally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "position of compression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "ankle inversion and plantar flexion (when traumatic)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pathoanatomy",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**intrinsic impingement**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**dorsal osteophytes over tibiotalar or talonavicular joints**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "other bony deformity (pes cavus, post-fracture)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "ganglion cyst",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tumor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendinitis or hypertrophic muscle belly of EHL, EDL or TA",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "peripheral edema",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "extrinsic impingement",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "tight laces or ski boots",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "high heels (induces plantar flexion)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "trauma (including recurrent ankle instability)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Associated conditions",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "pes cavus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "fracture",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "navicular nonunion",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "talonavicular arthritis",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "systemic conditions causing peripheral edema",
              "table": null,
